Yes, I wrote a AMD2901 cross assemble starting with the MIT Mical assembler.
It only took a few days. This was done on the Honeywell Level-6.  The guys
here in France are supporting this UNIX system that we developed.  Also,
Hoenywell in Belarica has it.  But it's so easy to do that it may be
easier to just start with the MIT mical assembler or perhaps a System5
assembler with COFF stuff.  Also, the 4BSD assembler seems nice in using
#defines, I am not sure if System 5 assembler can do that.  

	The guys to contact in France for the Mical assemblers are:

		lvbull!jim.uucp
		lvbull!cr
		lvbull!sylvain

	the stuff is burried Christian Reme's system, perhaps Jim
	has a copy.  It's been 5 years since I wrote it.
